      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC9962455::web::000::abstract"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "The starting CoCrFeNiTi solid solution has a chemically homogeneous lattice.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The starting CoCrFeNiTi alloy has little dislocation pinning or lattice-distortion-induced pinning.",
      "field": "hypothesis; material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The relative lack of dislocation pinning causes the starting alloy's moderate or relatively low hardness and strength.",
      "field": "hypothesis; mechanism; baseline",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The lack of nanoscale barriers permits easier dislocation glide and thereby produces good ductility.",
      "field": "hypothesis; mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The starting CoCrFeNiTi alloy has good machinability.",
      "field": "baseline",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Changing Ti content or synthesis conditions can alter the phases, microstructure, and mechanical properties of CoCrFeNiTix alloys.",
      "field": "intervention",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC9962455::web::000::abstract"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "A slight off-equimolar composition or suitable processing will induce nanoscale precipitates or chemical short-range order in CoCrFeNiTi.",
      "field": "intervention; structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC9962455::web::000::abstract"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "Nanoscale precipitates or chemical short-range order act as barriers to dislocation motion.",
      "field": "structural_mediator; mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Increasing the density of nanoscale obstacles raises the stress required for dislocation motion.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Induced nanoscale obstacles will increase the hardness and yield strength of modified CoCrFeNiTi relative to the equimolar starting alloy.",
      "field": "mechanism; predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC9962455::web::000::abstract"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "Increasing nanoscale obstacle density will increase strain hardening.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Strengthening by induced nanoscale obstacles may moderately reduce ductility without eliminating plasticity.",
      "field": "hypothesis; mechanism; predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The proposed mechanism applies from room temperature to approximately 600 °C under quasi-static loading.",
